{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"baa925c2686f57392083336656dee348d5ab89a03a0928a9be9e28f7a7a0308f","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM review kernel token limits","key_entities":["MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS","src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py","model_max_output_tokens","nova-pro","nova-2-lite","nova-lite","nova-micro","DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS","bedrock:us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0","us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0"],"problem_keywords":["bedrock","amazon nova","output tokens","model ceiling","validation error","llm"],"propositions":["Amazon Nova models on Bedrock have a 10,000 output token ceiling but MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS lacks entries for them, causing Bedrock to reject review calls with ValidationException.","The model_max_output_tokens lookup uses substring matching and must include explicit entries for nova-lite and nova-2-lite since the latter contains a hyphen separating the version number.","Plan-review calls using Nova models collapse to INDETERMINATE when token limits are exceeded, blocking end-to-end validation workflows.","Adding four Nova model entries (nova-pro, nova-2-lite, nova-lite, nova-micro) at 10,000 tokens unblocks Bedrock Nova inference without affecting existing Claude model behavior or the fallback default."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787886535041969001,"uuid":"2d4d90d4-6070-4e9f-8c95-b10109a3fc94"}